IDENTICAL: kernel ELF matches across Linux and Windows (bb25a012d22a7d76ba3ba5cf879cb521ad8cdc51ea27ae64b1a4b90f1b0d1ede)
IDENTICAL: nova.hdd matches across Linux and Windows (dc78a635be94898593ba4bd983d847b6a5b5fba665e4229a3b1622fd64a69ede)
RESULT: C5 cross-host reproducibility GATE PASSED

Are the hashed files the right ones? build-disk.sh embeds $KERNEL_ELF at
/NUCLEUS of the ESP and writes the blake2b-512 of that same file into
build/limine.conf.<image> (scripts/build-disk.sh, the C4 comment block), and
build/nova.hdd is the image those steps produce. So kernel.sha256 is the ELF
the kernel is loaded from, and image.sha256 is the whole disk. That is what the
commit message says is compared.

