P2  digest a file that does not exist -> CAUGHT, but by the Windows build job,
    not by the gate: run 42390125112

$ gh run view 42390125112
✓ build (ubuntu-latest) in 23s (ID 128455751987)
X build (windows-latest) in 30s (ID 128455752106)
  ✓ Build disk image (Windows)
  X Compute artifact digests
  - Upload Windows digests
  ✓ Post Run actions/checkout@v4

On Ubuntu the step survived and uploaded an empty digest:

sha256sum: kernel/target/x86_64-unknown-none/release/NUCLEUS-MISSING: No such file or directory
Linux kernel ELF SHA-256: Linux nova.hdd SHA-256:   f31499be981e3d5790ea4cd587b9ceb73055aeb34578c358456c1110497d72ca

On Windows the same step died:

sha256sum: kernel/target/x86_64-unknown-none/release/NUCLEUS-MISSING: No such file or directory
##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.

The two jobs run identical command text under different shells. Ubuntu's
implicit shell is "bash -e {0}", where a pipeline's status is awk's (0).
Windows uses "shell: bash", which GitHub expands to
"bash --noprofile --norc -eo pipefail {0}", so the sha256sum failure kills the
step. Because the Windows build failed, the compare job never ran. So the run
went red for a reason no one wrote down, and the gate itself was never asked.

P2 counts as CAUGHT under rule 15 (a check turned red), but it is not evidence
about the gate, which is why it turns into finding N1 rather than a pass mark.

